  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Provision of Life-Saving Essential Health Services and Outbreak Preparedness in Earthquake Affected Areas in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project targets 168,000 persons in the earthquake affected districts of Paktika and Khost provinces with the provision of basic health care and psychosocial support through the deployment of four temporary static basic health centers and four mobile health teams. The project will also support Infectious disease outbreak preparedness and prevention through the deployment of six community mobilizer teams for community sensitization and awareness on disease prevention, particularly acute watery diarrhea/Cholera, which is of particular risk in the disaster-affected area.</narrative>
  </description>
